\0
As the Freedom Guard grew in military strength, their political influence increased as well. The Freedom Guard negotiated a treaty with several outlying provincial governments, only marginally under Imperium control. This Pax Liberati, which was to be signed at a conference on Lycean,  would significantly improve their strategic position in the outlying sectors and increase the Freedom Guard's access to critical resources.\n\n
The Imperium was aware of the summit but did not wish to cement the alliance by attacking the involved worlds. Instead they duplicated a division of Freedom Guard troops and stormed Lycean in an attempt to make the conference appear to be a Freedom Guard ambush and splinter the coalition.
\1
Steal the plans for the Freedom Guard attack vehicles at the base on the outskirts of Lycean, then replicate their weapons and use them to raid the city and eliminate the citizen population. The attack will appear to be a Freedom Guard ambush. It will breed dissension among the anarchist factions, and they will tear each other apart like dogs. You must act quickly as they are preparing to sign the Pax Liberati even now.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Use your Infiltrators to steal plans for\n
\s\s\s\s Freedom Guard units and structures, then\n
\s\s\s\s form a Freedom Guard attack force\n
-->  Sabotage the treaty conference by\n
\s\s\s\s destroying the city before time runs out\n
\n\n
Tip: Morph your infiltrator into an enemy infantry unit so that you can enter his base without detection.  With the Infiltrator out of the enemy's line-of-sight, select the Infiltrator and press 'I' to get the morph cursor.  Click on the enemy infantry to morph into it.  Enter the enemy's HQ, Training Facility or Assembly Plant to steal plans for buildings and units.  Once you've obtained the plans, eject the Infiltrator from the building, and return him to your own HQ so that you can build the new technology.


\2
You gain in strength with every victory.\n 
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
Using Freedom Guard weapons, Imperium forces terrorized the city of Lycean, slaughtering much of the civilian population. Taken by surprise and confused by the attacking force's similar appearance to their own troops, the Freedom Guard was unable to drive out the invaders before much of the city was ravaged. The treaty conference was abandoned, and the Freedom Guard was unable to seal their alliance with the rim worlds.
\3
Your lack of skill cannot be tolerated.

